# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit: per-device data and proprietary firmware.
# EFS/persist/GPT dumps carry identifiers unique to one phone (IMEI, BT/WiFi
# MAC, disk GUIDs); Qualcomm/Samsung firmware is not redistributable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
capture/
backups/
firmware-q2q/
rescue/gpt/
rescue/gpt-adb/
rescue/out/
*.img
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tar.md5
# generic 2 KiB BCB images used by the force-recovery procedure: keep
!rescue/misc-boot-recovery.img
!rescue/misc-cleared.img
# board data / NVM blobs (Samsung's, or regenerable from linux-firmware with
# bt-work/bdf/mkboard2.py)
*.bin
*.elf
bdwlan.elf*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Re-creatable sources: tools/setup-sources.sh fetches and patches these.
# linux/, linux-fedora/, uniloader/ are tracked as submodules instead (pinned
# upstream commit only -- the patches/ and *-work/ dirs still carry the deltas).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
initramfs-work/busybox-src/
initramfs-work/busybox.tar.bz2
vendor-src/lrzsz-extract/
vendor-src/lrzsz-build/
# DIAG/EFS2 work: upstream checkouts, not ours. andersson/diag is built ON the
# phone (see HANDBOOK 35.2.1); qrtr supplies libqrtr.h; QCSuper is the EFS2
# protocol reference. tools/setup-sources.sh diag re-fetches all three.
modem-work/diag/
modem-work/qrtr/
modem-work/qcsuper/
# Samsung GPL source drop -- large, retrievable from opensource.samsung.com
SM-F926B/Kernel/
SM-F926B/Platform/
SM-F926B/Baseband/
# Stock Fedora image and everything unpacked or staged from it
*.raw.xz
rootfs-build/fedora-aarch64/
rootfs-work/fedora-mobile/
rootfs-work/modules-stage/
rootfs-work/adsp-fw/
rootfs-work/stage/
rootfs-work/inspect/
rootfs-work/extract.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build outputs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# kbuild (out-of-tree modules)
*.o
*.ko
*.mod
*.mod.c
*.cmd
*.dtb
modules.order
Module.symvers
# initramfs
*.cpio.gz
*.cpio.gz.*
initramfs-work/bin/
initramfs-work/init
initramfs-work/root/
initramfs-work/*.spec
initramfs-work/busybox-build.log
# misc
__pycache__/
*.pyc
#---
# Look, we know what I used, I just don't wanna share this one folder.
.claude/
